<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Novellae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Novellae, or Novels, are the new laws issued by the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> after the completion of his legal code. Together with the Codex, Digest and Institutes they form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a>. This codification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>, a landmark of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, later became a foundation of European legal traditions.</p></div>
